## (a) What evidence Vanta requires for this control
Standard SOC 2 CC 6.1 "system access restricted to authorized access only" — Vanta satisfies this by mapping a mix of:
- **Access Control Policy** (policy document defining provisioning, least privilege, RBAC, review, deprovisioning).
- **Automated tests** proving access is technically restricted, e.g.: SSO/identity-provider access managed, MFA enforced, unique accounts, role-based/least-privilege access, access removed on offboarding, server/production access restricted to authorized personnel, idle-session timeout.
- **Documents** evidencing access is reviewed/granted by process, e.g.: periodic access review, access request ticket & history.

Because it's a Vanta-**Source** control (not integration-auto-evaluated on its own), it is considered "passing" once the relevant tests/documents/policy are **mapped** to it and those items pass.

